  "platform_limits": [
    "Executed on Linux x86_64 with descriptor-relative no-symlink file access and flock; other native platforms are not qualified. Platforms without guarded reads retain metadata-only maps and refuse search.",
    "Index snapshots are closed artifacts. Legacy journal/WAL/SHM sidecars are refused without recovery or deletion. Remap into a new output after stopping the legacy writer.",
    "Publication serializes cooperating Repo Graph writers through one persistent lock inode. Arbitrary external in-place SQLite writers are unsupported; sidecars and mutation during copy are rejected.",
    "Readers stream one private disk copy per artifact revision and reuse it for warm queries. Cold copy cost, peak disk and large-repository resource limits remain unmeasured.",
    "Atomic replace is the publication point. Directory fsync failure reports published data with uncertain crash durability; it does not claim rollback.",
    "Product writers finish statements before publication. A writer closed with an active UPDATE RETURNING cursor is refused without publishing; arbitrary unfinished DBAPI write-cursor lifecycles are not qualified."
  ],
